e  custom class was the pathetic  hk21 this lmg suffers from the usual  fault of a weapon of its size  slow run speed dismal aim downsides time  but to make it worse the hk had the  jumpiest recoil i recall from that  entire game  other guns with high recoil veer left  right and up  predictable patterns right the hk21 does  all of the above to make matters worse  four of its five optional attachments  are scopes  scopes on a gun this slow and jumpy  scopes only make the experience  worse but for some players any scope  tops the unusually small iron sights  also if you choose a scope you're stuck  with a lousy 30 round magazine  is there a foregrip no is there a bipod  in the picture is there a reason to use  this no  way the only redeeming quality it sounds  cool i guess  on paper the hs10 looks like it would be  a fun addition it sounds cool  it has a unique design and it fits the  whole espionage theme of the first black  ops game  it's even teased as an alluring  classified weapon that can only be  unlocked after every other shotgun had  been unlocked first  when you do get your hands on it you'll  come to find that it is an incredibly  underwhelming shotgun even by shotgun  standards the hs10's range  is pathetic and to rub salt into that  wound you start with a max ammo of 4  bullets so prepare to hide a lot or lose  a lot  its only attachment is dual wielding  which strips you of the ability to aim  down sights  and aiming down sights is the only thing  that made it barely usable in the first  place  may i suggest the spas 12 instead  if you've played 2019's modern warfare  at all in the last year  you'll know the growl 556 launched in  season 2  and continually patched until season 4  the growl was an overpowered laser beam  especially in war zone with the right  attachments this thing became the acr  from modern warfare 2 with higher damage  the amount of people using damascus camo  on the grouse was ridiculous  this gun was worth grinding for and the  only 